# Custom cell library for ABC technology mapping.
# This is the small file that tells ABC: "please map the circuit using IMPLY."
# It follows the SIMPLER/Ben-Hur 2020 flow, but swaps the NOR target for IMPLY.
#
# IMPLY(a, b) = !a + b   (material implication, the only compute primitive)
# INV is kept as a pseudo-gate while ABC is mapping. The sequencer later turns
# NOT x into:
#     FALSE work_cell
#     IMPLY x -> work_cell
# so INV gets area 2, not 1.
#
# The PIN numbers are mostly legal-looking placeholders. This project uses
# ABC's area mapper, not its timing model, so the area field above is the part
# that matters for this experiment.

GATE IMPLY  1  O=!a+b;     PIN * UNKNOWN 1 999 1 0 1 0
GATE INV    2  O=!a;       PIN * UNKNOWN 1 999 1 0 1 0
GATE ZERO   0  O=CONST0;
GATE ONE    0  O=CONST1;
